=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, ribonn TE, skeletal_muscle ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.0117
  lasso keeps 43 of 61 codons; sets 18 to exactly 0: TTT, TTG, TCG, TAT, TGT, TGC, CTG, CCC, CGT, ATC, ATA, ACA, AAC, AAA, AGA, GTA, GTG, GGG
  of those 18, 18 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 51 nominally significant codons overall, 33 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9806, Spearman rho = 0.9772; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.875 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS -83.181 / 5.935, lasso -0.596 / 5.207
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS 85.0596, lasso 2.5056

[2] Fit on 4,650 autosomal training genes
